- 2026-10-28 03:47 UTC: Step 1, first part: commands on the bus, with the bus on. The `COMMANDS` stream is a work queue with a subject for each rig and at most 100 waiting for each (`core/link/commands.ts`); control publishes each signed command once its store has it, and takes it off when the owner cancels it; the supervisor takes its rig's one at a time, delivers each to its harness as before and acks it once control has the outcome; one delivered already, expired or for another rig is acked and not delivered; the HTTP poll stays as a fallback every 3 minutes. Against a real server a command went from issued to delivered in about 54 ms. A refused report page heals: control's answer to the supervisor's regular call names its place in the rig's reports, and a supervisor still ahead of it a round later goes back and sends one page a round. Left in step 1: each rig's own key on the bus and its permissions (question 2), and a check of the commands in the compose smoke.
