- 2026-10-28 13:37 UTC: Control's pages read views kept up to date as events arrive. Control's views are a folder (goal 125's T8), and a rig's fold is a class that takes one event at a time; control keeps one for each rig and its current ledger (`control/views/cache.ts`), and each read folds only the events since the last (a look at the newest seq first, then the same lean read as before), with a full reset's new ledger starting a new fold and a retired rig's dropped. What the fold holds for good is frozen, and each read copies the rest, so no caller's change reaches it. Measured with `trial_started`, `trial_finished` and `journal_note` events (a third each), median of 5:

  | Events | Before (every read folds all) | First read | Read, nothing new | Read after 100 new | A kept fold's heap |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 50,000 | 151 ms | 157 ms | 0.41 ms | 2.3 ms | 5.3 MiB |
  | 100,000 | 366 ms | 382 ms | 0.66 ms | 4.1 ms | 10.4 MiB |
  | 200,000 | 1,035 ms | 1,045 ms | 1.2 ms | 8.6 ms | 20.6 MiB |

  The first read is mostly the store's read, not the fold (332 ms and 15 ms at 100,000 events): `store.events` walks the rig's index again for each page of 5,000. An index on the rig's ledger and seq, or pages by seq, would cut it; that is for the store's split.
